Sentinela
Third-party code adapted into this repository is listed here with its licence.
- web/src/lib/player.ts implements the go2rtc WebSocket signalling / MSE
  protocol, following the behaviour of go2rtc's www/video-rtc.js.
  go2rtc: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Alexey Khit (AlexxIT).
  https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc

- The web app loads @hevcjs/core on demand (H.265 converted to H.264 in
  the browser for viewing, ADR-0026). MIT License, lid-labs.
  https://github.com/lid-labs/hevc.js

Runtime dependencies (not bundled in the binary): go2rtc (MIT, AlexxIT),
FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL, Debian package inside the container image).

The published server image (ghcr.io/luker2dw/sentinela) contains Debian
packages, among them FFmpeg and its libraries under the GPL/LGPL. Their
complete corresponding source is available from the Debian archive for the
same package versions (https://sources.debian.org, or `apt-get source
ffmpeg` on the image's Debian release); the versions are listed in the
image's SBOM attached to each release.

Object detector image (detector/, ADR-0016), built locally, not
redistributed: ONNX Runtime (MIT, Microsoft), PyAV (BSD-3-Clause) with its
bundled FFmpeg (LGPL), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause). The model is Ultralytics
YOLO26n (AGPL-3.0): the weights are downloaded (pinned by sha256) and
exported to ONNX while building the image; no weights or Ultralytics code
are part of this repository. detector/detector.py is original code; its
YOLO output decoding follows the public output format documented by
Ultralytics and Frigate's "yolo-generic" model type.
Bundled web fonts: Barlow and Barlow Semi Condensed (SIL Open Font License 1.1,
Jeremy Tribby), via @fontsource.

